// A logical operator or an ordering refused for its operands: the text and the kind.
//
// GLB-091 (decided 2026-10-05): `&&`, `||` and `!` on something that is not a
// Bool, and an ordering between two types that never compare, are a wrong TYPE —
// a `##Type` (D1). They were `##_` in the three engines.
//
// A string against a number is another case: `"5" < 10` compares, because the
// text is a number. `"a" < 10` fails on the VALUE of the text, so its message
// names the value, and its kind is not decided yet (GLB-094): this golden holds
// what the three engines answer today.
//
// `id` only hides each value's type from the analysers.

id(v) { <~ v }
n = id(10)
si = id(#1)
vacio = id(##_)
lista = id([1])
cinco = id("5")
letra = id("a")

!? { r1 = n && #1      >> r1 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
!? { r2 = #0 || vacio  >> r2 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
!? { r3 = !n           >> r3 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
!? { r4 = si < n       >> r4 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
!? { r5 = vacio < n    >> r5 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
!? { r6 = lista < lista >> r6 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
>> (cinco < n) ¶
!? { r7 = letra < n    >> r7 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
!? { r8 = n < letra    >> r8 ¶ } :! { >> _err ¶ }
